{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789555189,"nonce":"stDC4xERkrSrP7H7LVswwg/f2IU=","title":"LLVM entry promotion cannot retain structured Python objects","message":"Python tree.py leaks roughly one allocation per iteration when LLVM promotes build and check$trusted, whose signatures contain structured Node pointers. Skipping either promotion reduces but does not eliminate the growth; skipping LLVM entry promotion for structured pointer signatures restores bounded memory in the full pressure suite. The guard is in compile_at_tier and leaves scalar signatures eligible. Teach LLVM entry codegen to preserve collector ownership across calls and returns for structured pointers, then remove the guard and verify memory_pressure with ZYPY_LLVM=1 plus the checked speed kernels.","files":null}]}